#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
GUI-enabled copy of the fast Pockels chip mapping automation.

The original pockels_fast_map_automation.py is intentionally left untouched.
This file keeps the same CLI workflow under --cli and adds a Tkinter launcher
that monitors the generated progress/CSV files while the copied automation runs
in a child process.

This is the operator-facing fast-map workflow described in document.md.  It
reuses the hardware bring-up, alignment, Arduino routing, SMU safety, optical
calibration loading, and cleanup code from pockels_full_automation.py, but
replaces the slow full analyser sweep at each HWP with a fast adaptive check:

    local null plus a_null +/- 45 deg on every pixel
    balanced joint complex-EO/DC-derivative fit on the first pixel at every HWP
    the same fit on later pixels only when their triplet is inconclusive

Default run shape:
    83 selected chip pixels x 9 HWP angles x local background/+45/-45
    reads at 9 Vpp, followed by centre-dense DC hysteresis on the same pixels
    using a separate 4 Vpp gated small-signal probe

Default production safeguards:
    - 180 s DC poling dwell at the start of each pixel
    - stored QWP/ANL seed nulls with leakage checks
    - fast rotator readback with one corrective retry if outside tolerance

For an explicit AC-linearity diagnostic, run with --voltages 1,3,5,9.
"""

